// SET: `airfield` for "Armor Where Nobody Shot" (a wartime bomber airfield, early 1940s, no place name, no real unit).
// The MAIN module of the ONE connected world. Every place of film.json names it ("set": "airfield"); places differ only in light.
// Contract: episodes/armor-no-holes/SET_MAP.md v1 (every number below is from it). Story list: sets/airfield_STORY.md. Dressing: sets/airfield_DRESSING.md.
// It builds zone A (the hero bomber's spot), zone C (the parking row, tally board, tower side) and the far world (grass, runway, huts, trees,
// hills, sky), and JOINS two modules written by other departments, both guarded (a missing or throwing module gives a named STANDIN_ so this always loads):
//   ./bomber.js  buildBomber(THREE, ctx, { hero, damage, name, lod }) -> { group, anchors, set(state) }   local frame, nose +X, origin = wing centre on the ground
//   ./hangar.js  buildHangar(THREE, scene, film, ctx)               -> { update(f, state), anchors }    world coordinates
//   ./props.js   buildLantern(THREE, opt)                           -> { group, ... } or an Object3D    the Chief's amber lantern
// Plan coordinates: metres, Z up, cameras at negative Y looking toward +Y. Sun travels [+8, +4.5, -4.6].
// Movers (film.places.<place>.events = [{ f0, f1, obj, from, to }], smootherstep, last value held, first `from` before the first event;
// static values per place: film.places.<place>.state = { mover: value }):
//   mine:   tally 0..9 · landers 0..9 · taxi (x of the shredded-tail bomber on the lane y = LANE_Y = 18, held to x <= -17) · lantern [x, y, z] (its BASE point) · stepladder [x, y, z]
//   bomber: chalk, panel, patch, armor_here, plate_on, props (1 = stopped), finger_ring  ->  hero.set(state)
//   hangar: plates, needle, map, pin_boxes, calendar, barrel_lid, sun_sweep (and the whole state)  ->  hangar.update(f, state)
